  "rulesTitle": "How to Play (Rules)",
  "rulesClose": "Close",
  "rulesUnderstandButton": "GOT IT",
  "rulesSection1Title": "🃏 1. Deck, Deal & Drawing",
  "rulesSection1Body": "• Played with 106 cards: 2 full standard decks (104 cards) + 2 Printed Jokers.\n• Each player is dealt 10 cards.\n• Drawing is ONLY allowed from the closed stock pile. Drawing from the discard pile is not permitted.",
  "rulesSection2Title": "👑 2. Jokers (Indicator & Printed Jokers)",
  "rulesSection2Body": "• The Indicator card revealed after dealing determines the \"Wild Joker\" rank for the round.\n• All 8 cards of that rank across both decks + 2 Printed Jokers create 10 total jokers.\n• Jokers can represent any missing card in sets and runs.\n• 3 or more Jokers can form an independent valid meld on their own.\n• ATTENTION: Any unmelded Joker left in hand at round end incurs a heavy 25-point penalty!",
  "rulesSection3Title": "📐 3. Valid Melds (Sets and Runs)",
  "rulesSection3Body": "Cards are grouped into melds of at least 3 cards:\n• Set (Group): At least 3 or 4 cards of the SAME rank in DIFFERENT suits (e.g. ♠K, ♦K, ♣K). Duplicate suits in the same set are invalid.\n• Run (Sequence): At least 3 consecutive cards of the SAME suit (e.g. ♥7, ♥8, ♥9, ♥10).\n• Ace (A): May be used low (A-2-3) or high (J-Q-K-A); round-the-corner sequences (K-A-2) are invalid.",
  "rulesSection4Title": "🏆 4. Declaring and Going Out",
  "rulesSection4Body": "• On your turn, draw 1 card to hold 11 cards.\n• Arrange your 10 cards into valid melds and discard your 11th card to declare and win the round.\n• The player who declares a valid hand scores 0 PENALTY points.\n• Other players receive penalty points equal to the total value of their unmelded deadwood cards.",
  "rulesSection5Title": "💡 5. Example Winning Hand",
  "rulesSection5Body": "10 melded cards + 1 discard card:\n• Rack Row 1: [♠8, ♥8, ♦8] (3-Card Set)\n• Rack Row 2: [♣4, ♣5, ♣6, ♣7] (4-Card Run)\n• Rack Row 3: [♥J, ♥Q, ♥K] (3-Card Run)\n• Discard Card: [♦2] (11th leftover card discarded to table)\nResult: 10 cards fully melded, 11th card discarded to finish successfully!",
  "rulesSection6Title": "✨ 6. Assisted Mode vs 🔥 Expert Mode",
  "rulesSection6Body": "• Assisted Mode: Valid melds are marked with green badges (✓ MELD) and deadwood penalty points are calculated in real time. Winning discard candidates are suggested.\n• Expert Mode: No meld or penalty hints! You must arrange your rack manually.\n• WARNING (False Finish): Declaring an invalid hand in Expert Mode instantly burns you with a 101 PENALTY, while all other players receive 0 penalty!",
  "rulesSection7Title": "🔢 7. Penalties and the 101 Threshold",
  "rulesSection7Body": "Penalty values for unmelded deadwood cards:\n• Ace (A) = 10 points\n• Face cards (K, Q, J) = 10 points\n• Number cards (2..10) = Face value\n• Joker = 25 points\n• Reaching 101 or more cumulative penalty points ELIMINATES (busts) the player from the table.",
  "rulesSection8Title": "🔄 8. Stock Exhaustion (Draw)",
  "rulesSection8Body": "• If the 106-card stock pile is exhausted and nobody has declared, the round ends in a draw.\n• All players receive penalty points for their unmelded cards.",
  "rulesSection9Title": "🥇 9. Table Champion",
  "rulesSection9Body": "• Yanık is a survival game. Opponents are eliminated as they bust past 101 penalty points.\n• The last remaining player standing below 101 points is crowned the TABLE CHAMPION!",

